---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Imperial Knights Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to Imperial Knights? Learn how this walking-tank faction plays, how to paint their heraldic armor, and what to buy first for a 3–5 model army."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions/" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">🏰</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Imperial Knights</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            A complete army in three to five models. Noble pilots in fifty-foot war machines
            striding across the battlefield, each one a walking fortress with a name,
            a lineage, and a legacy stretching back ten thousand years.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Walking Tanks</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-red-400">Hard</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$250+</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">Who are the Imperial Knights?</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          Long before the Imperium as we know it, the ancient colonists of humanity spread
          across the stars in great generation ships. On many worlds, their technology slowly
          degraded. The vast walking war machines they brought with them — the Knights —
          became the only defense against alien predators and hostile environments. The
          families who maintained and piloted these machines became noble houses, their
          bloodlines and their war engines intertwined for ten thousand years.
        </p>
        <p>
          A Knight is not just a weapon — it is an heirloom. Each machine has a name.
          Each has a heraldic history painted on its armored panels. The pilot, called
          a Freeblade if operating alone or a Knight of the House if part of a household,
          forms a deep bond with their machine through a device called the Throne Mechanicum.
          They experience the memories of every previous pilot who ever sat in that same seat.
          They carry the weight of generations.
        </p>
        <p>
          Armiger-class Knights are the smaller variants — fifteen to twenty feet tall,
          piloted by young noble aspirants who have not yet proven themselves worthy of a
          full Knight. They serve as escorts and screens for the larger machines. Full
          Questoris-class Knights are the main battle walkers — fifty feet of armored fury
          carrying enough firepower to level a fortress. And then there are the Dominus-class,
          the largest of all, so heavily armed they change the shape of a battle simply by
          being present.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each great household — House Terryn, House Griffith, House Hawkshroud, among others
          — has its own colors, heraldry, and battlefield traditions. Or you can create
          your own Household, designing the heraldry from scratch. Few things in the hobby
          are as visually striking as a fully painted Imperial Knight army.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          A full Imperial Knights army might have <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">three to five models
          total</strong>. That is the entire army. Every single activation matters enormously
          because you have so few of them. A single Knight Questoris can shoot multiple
          weapons simultaneously, stomp infantry underfoot in melee, and absorb an extraordinary
          amount of punishment before going down.
        </p>
        <p>
          Armigers — the smaller Armiger Warglaives and Helverins — function as your screens
          and objective holders. They're faster than full Knights and can get into positions
          the larger machines can't. A typical starting force of three Armigers plus one
          full Knight is both visually impressive and mechanically solid.
        </p>
        <p>
          The rules are simpler per-model than most infantry armies. You're not tracking
          the interactions of thirty different unit abilities. But each decision carries
          enormous weight — moving a Knight in the wrong direction, or misjudging an
          opponent's threat, can lose the game. The army is mechanically accessible but
          punishing of strategic errors. Not recommended for complete beginners from a
          competitive standpoint, but one of the most visually spectacular forces to own.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">Imperial Knights are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You want the most visually spectacular army in 40k</li>
            <li>✓ You love big centerpiece models over painting hordes</li>
            <li>✓ You enjoy creating heraldic paint schemes and house identity</li>
            <li>✓ You want fewer models but massive impact per model</li>
            <li>✓ You love the feudal-noble lore and machine-spirit bonds</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You want to learn the game before spending $250+</li>
            <li>✗ You enjoy painting lots of smaller infantry models</li>
            <li>✗ You want to field a horde army</li>
            <li>✗ You're not ready to tackle large flat panels with an airbrush</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Imperial Knights</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Honest warning: large flat armor panels are more challenging than detailed infantry.
        Every brush stroke shows. An airbrush makes this significantly easier.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Build and prime in sub-assemblies</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Keep the armor panels separate from the skeleton. Spray the skeleton Leadbelcher (metallic), then prime the armor panels separately in your chosen house color. Sub-assemblies are not optional — they're the difference between a clean model and a nightmare.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Base coat the armor panels</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">House Terryn = Macragge Blue. House Griffith = Mephiston Red. House Hawkshroud = Averland Sunset. Or invent your own house — the colors are yours. An airbrush gives smooth results on large flat surfaces; brush painting works but requires patience and thin coats.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Heraldic panel divisions (optional but stunning)</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">The classic Knight look divides armor panels diagonally or quartered — one half in the house color, one half in a second color (often black or white). Use masking tape to get clean straight lines before painting the second color. This is the signature Imperial Knights aesthetic.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Paint the skeleton and mechanical details</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Leadbelcher on the iron frame, joints, and mechanical components. Wash with Nuln Oil for depth. Balthasar Gold on pistons and decorative elements. This is the part that goes quickly — it's the armor panels that take the time.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Edge highlight the armor panels</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A thin bright line around every armor plate edge in a lighter version of your house color. This is what makes the model "pop" on the table. For blue: Calgar Blue. For red: Evil Sunz Scarlet. Take your time — each panel edge matters.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">6</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Add transfers, heraldic symbols, weathering</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">GW provides decal sheets with Knight heraldry. Apply them with Microsol and Microset for best results. Then add battle damage: chip effects with a sponge, rust streaks, soot stains around weapon barrels. These machines have fought for centuries.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Airbrush tip -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">Should you get an airbrush?</h3>
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          For Imperial Knights, an airbrush is more useful than almost any other faction.
          Large flat panels are where brush strokes show most — an airbrush lays smooth,
          even coats effortlessly. A basic entry-level airbrush kit (around $60–$80) will
          transform how these models look. It's not required, but if you're committed to
          Knights, it's worth the investment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-4 text-lg">There is no official Combat Patrol box for Imperial Knights.</p>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10">Start with three Armigers — they're the backbone of any Knight force and the fastest way into the faction. Then add a full Knight once you've got them painted.</p>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$128 for 2 Armigers · buy 2 boxes for 4 Armigers</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Armiger Warglaives (box of 2)</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-3 leading-relaxed">
          The smaller, faster Knights — 15–20 feet tall, piloted by young noble aspirants.
          Each box builds 2 Armigers that also assemble as Armiger Helverins (ranged variant).
          Start with two boxes (4 Armigers) for a solid core force that can hold objectives
          and screen your eventual full Knight.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Armigers are also the best model to practice your house color scheme on before
          committing it to a full Knight. Mistakes on a smaller model are more forgiving.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=armiger+warglaives+imperial+knights+warhammer+40k&tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon for Armiger Warglaives →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$160 · the centrepiece</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Knight Questoris</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          The iconic full Knight — builds as multiple variants including the Knight Paladin,
          Knight Errant, Knight Gallant, and more depending on weapon loadout. This single
          kit is the centerpiece of your army. With three or four Armigers flanking it,
          you have a complete, competitive Imperial Knights force.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=knight+questoris+imperial+warhammer+40k&tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Knight households -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Choose your Knight Household</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'House Terryn', color: 'Blue and white', desc: 'Aggressive, honor-bound warriors. Classic bold blue with white and red accents. The most iconic Knight household.' },
            { name: 'House Griffith', color: 'Red and white', desc: 'Proud and fierce. Red armor with gold trim. Slightly easier to paint than blue — red is more forgiving.' },
            { name: 'House Hawkshroud', color: 'Yellow and black', desc: 'Honor-sworn defenders, never abandon allies. Yellow armor — challenging to paint but striking.' },
            { name: 'House Cadmus', color: 'Green and bone', desc: 'Battle-hardened veterans. Darker green scheme, excellent for weathering and battle damage effects.' },
            { name: 'Freeblade (custom)', color: 'Your choice', desc: 'A Knight who owes allegiance to no house. Design your own colors and heraldry from scratch. Total creative freedom.' },
          ].map(house => (
            <div class="bg-[#111113] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
              <div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-3 mb-1">
                <h4 class="font-display font-semibold">{house.name}</h4>
                <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">{house.color}</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">{house.desc}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need (House Terryn example)</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Macragge Blue Spray', use: 'Main armor color — covers large panels fast', required: true },
            { name: 'Abaddon Black', use: 'Heraldic divisions and secondary panels', required: true },
            { name: 'Leadbelcher', use: 'Metallic skeleton, joints, mechanical details', required: true },
            { name: 'Nuln Oil', use: 'Shade wash over all metallic areas', required: true },
            { name: 'Balthasar Gold + Agrax Earthshade', use: 'Gold pistons, trim, ornate details', required: true },
            { name: 'Calgar Blue', use: 'Edge highlights on blue armor panels', required: true },
            { name: 'White Scar', use: 'White heraldic panels and checks', required: false },
            { name: 'Mephiston Red', use: 'Red heraldic details and eye lenses', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: '2x Armiger Warglaives boxes (4 Armigers)', cost: '~$128', note: 'Your core troops and objective holders' },
          { item: '1x Knight Questoris (full Knight)', cost: '~$160', note: 'The centrepiece of your force' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (7–8)', cost: '~$45', note: 'Spray + metallics + shade + house color + trim' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$15', note: 'Texture paint + tufts + larger rocks for big bases' },
          { item: 'Masking tape (for heraldry)', cost: '~$8', note: 'Critical for clean heraldic panel divisions' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase' },
          { item: 'Plastic glue', cost: '~$8', note: 'Plastic glue is better than superglue for large kits' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">All-in starter total</p>
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-[#c9a84c] text-lg">~$384</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
        Prices approximate. Imperial Knights are the most expensive faction to start but among
        the cheapest to complete — you need only a handful of kits total. The painting time
        per model is high, but you only have five models. Budget for an airbrush if you can.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold mb-4">For House and Honor.</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg mb-8">
        Three Armigers. One Knight. That's your army. Paint them slowly, paint them well —
        and when that Knight strides onto the table for the first time, you'll understand
        why people collect Imperial Knights.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a
          href="/painting"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display tracking-wide"
        >
          Painting Guide →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/quiz"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Retake the Quiz
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
